  "id": "user-centered-design",
  "term": "user-centered design",
  "definition": "User-centered design is an iterative way of developing a product or intervention in close collaboration with the people who will use it, so the end result fits their needs. It typically involves analyzing the problem and users’ needs, creating and revising a prototype, and evaluating it in real-life use.",
